# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.83, opened by scripts/new_cut.sh from v1.0.82.
#
# WHY THESE PINS:
#   v1.0.82 shipped and walked and its usage_journal_producers row could 
#   never have moved, because two of the roster's five producers were not in 
#   that artefact at all. This cut ships both, plus the one measured 
#   install-log error class from that walk. THREE THINGS IN THE ARTEFACT: the 
#   cm048 producer re-vendored at CM048 53fcdf0b (CM051 #1881), which also 
#   took the vendored tree from 1142 undescribed divergence lines to zero; 
#   the cm041 producer grafted into the vendored contact_syncer and 
#   assistant_api as ADDED LINES ONLY (CM051 #1884), which ships it without 
#   moving a pin that sits thirteen commits before the upstream PII scrub; 
#   and the store-auth .pth import guard (CM051 #1886), which stops three 
#   ModuleNotFoundError tracebacks that install_error_honesty rightly failed 
#   on while every step reported status=ok. THE DAEMON DOES NOT MOVE: 0.4.77 
#   at a9af0595, so no re-pin and the six pin sites are untouched. NOT 
#   FORECAST CLEAN, and the reasons are measured rather than hoped: 
#   usage_journal_producers reaches 4 of 5 at best, because cm044's summary 
#   backfill wrote nothing in twenty minutes with no process alive and both 
#   its agents exiting 0, so the fifth row needs the backfill to actually run 
#   rather than the walk to wait longer; pwg_preferences is diagnosed as 
#   structural, the tool reading an hourly-compiled interest profile that 
#   predates the seed; people_count_agreement and people_stores_reconcile 
#   turn on whether the re-sweep prunes 21 vectors whose Person the graph no 
#   longer has, which is undetermined; and the fact_missing residual is model 
#   behaviour. Under decision A the verdict rule stands.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.84, opened by scripts/new_cut.sh from v1.0.83.
#
# WHY THESE PINS:
#   v1.0.83 WAS TAGGED ONCE AT db531954 AND BUILT NOTHING. Its cut refused at 
#   step 8, Build sign notarise staple, inside make check-manifest, on ONE 
#   red out of 17 PASS 1 FAIL 54 SKIP 0 CANNOT-RUN: the no-operator-hostname 
#   row, one hit of the operator's personal box hostname in the payload copy 
#   of the vendor manifest. Steps 10, 11 and 12 then failed for want of a 
#   dist DMG, so that was ONE defect and not four, and the gate was RIGHT: an 
#   operator identifier in a shipped file of a PUBLIC product is exactly what 
#   it exists to stop. v1.0.84 CARRIES THE v1.0.83 PAYLOAD UNCHANGED PLUS THE 
#   ONE FIX THAT UNBLOCKS IT, so the three producer and guard rows get their 
#   first chance to be measured on a box. FOUR THINGS IN THE ARTEFACT: the 
#   cm048 producer re-vendored at CM048 53fcdf0b (CM051 #1881), which also 
#   took the vendored tree from 1142 undescribed divergence lines to zero; 
#   the cm041 producer grafted into the vendored contact_syncer and 
#   assistant_api as ADDED LINES ONLY (CM051 #1884), which ships it without 
#   moving a pin that sits thirteen commits before the upstream PII scrub; 
#   the store-auth .pth import guard (CM051 #1886), net line delta zero so 
#   the fifteen absolute citations in the re-arm comment cannot shift; and 
#   NEW FOR THIS CUT the reword that removes the operator identifier from 
#   vendor/VENDOR_MANIFEST.toml (CM051 #1894), which gui/Makefile:1249 copies 
#   into the .app verbatim, together with the PR-time test that holds that 
#   file to the cut's own no-operator rules by READING them out of 
#   permanent.yaml rather than declaring a second copy of the identifier to 
#   work with. THE GUARD GAP IS THE PART THAT RECURS: the pattern that 
#   stopped v1.0.83 existed and could only fire at cut time, because the 
#   PR-time scanner has no hostname alternative in its master pattern, so 
#   every check on #1881 was green AND truthful and a version number was 
#   spent to learn it. THE DAEMON DOES NOT MOVE: 0.4.77 at a9af0595, no 
#   re-pin, the six pin sites untouched, so the same-filename hazard between 
#   the two release repos does not arise this cut. THE WALK INSTRUMENT HAS 
#   MOVED EVEN THOUGH THE ARTEFACT HAS NOT, and the two must not be confused: 
#   CM051 #1887 (the ingest_coverage NEVER-RAN arm and the wiped-box baseline 
#   reset), #1888 (the preference seed kickstarts the hourly compile and 
#   reads the subject back through the API the tool reads) and #1890 (after 
#   the seeds, kickstart the wiki recompile and WAIT for its summary 
#   backfill) are all in the checkout the walk runs from and in NO DMG, 
#   because gui/project.yml bundles box_walk_probes zero times. A probe that 
#   moves because the instrument was wrong is a real move and it is not a 
#   product improvement. NOT FORECAST CLEAN, and the reasons are measured 
#   rather than hoped: usage_journal_producers reaches 4 of 5 on the artefact 
#   alone, and 5 ONLY IF the backfill #1890 kickstarts actually writes, which 
#   is the open question rather than a prediction, because on the v1.0.82 box 
#   that backfill launched at 18:48:11Z, wrote 0 bytes, and was still 0 bytes 
#   twenty minutes later with no process alive and both agents exiting 0; 
#   people_count_agreement and people_stores_reconcile turn on whether the 
#   re-sweep prunes the 21 vectors whose Person the graph no longer has, 
#   which is undetermined with hydrate-people.log absent; and the 
#   fact_missing residual is model behaviour, which no cut fixes. Under 
#   decision A the verdict rule stands: if every other probe passes and 
#   usage_journal_producers does not, the record reads FAILED.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.85, opened by scripts/new_cut.sh from v1.0.84.
#
# WHY THESE PINS:
#   THREE VERSION NUMBERS HAVE NOW BEEN SPENT ON STEP 8 AND THEY DIED AT 
#   THREE DIFFERENT GATES, which is why this is progress and not a loop. 
#   v1.0.83 died at check-manifest on an operator hostname in a file this 
#   repo ships, 17 PASS 1 FAIL. v1.0.84 PASSED check-manifest at 18 PASS 0 
#   FAIL, the hit going 1 to 0 and the PASS count up by exactly one, which 
#   proves CM051 #1894 DELIVERED on the ARTEFACT rather than on main; it then 
#   died one gate later at check-freshness, on vendor:cm041/contact_syncer 
#   lagging a0f3ca19 with no covering hold_ack, fresh=14 held=8 exempt=4 
#   stale/RED=1. v1.0.85 CARRIES THE v1.0.84 PAYLOAD UNCHANGED PLUS THE ACK 
#   THAT CLEARS IT. a0f3ca19 is CM041 #161, an upstream scrub of a comment in 
#   contact_syncer that named two real people; it landed AFTER the v1.0.82 
#   cut ran and v1.0.83 never reached that gate, so nothing regressed: a new 
#   upstream commit arrived and no ack covered it. THE ACK STATES A MEASURED 
#   FACT AND NOT A PREFERENCE, and the gate's own text draws that line. 
#   Measured on the SCRUB COMMIT ALONE rather than the 55-commit span, which 
#   mixes in everything else: the scrub changes exactly 2 lines of the 
#   vendored file-set, both PRE-scrub lines are ABSENT from the vendored copy 
#   and both POST-scrub lines are PRESENT, compared by line digest so no name 
#   is reproduced to run the check, with a CONTROL that 425 of 533 long 
#   UNCHANGED lines from the same file at the same commit ARE found, because 
#   "both absent" and "the comparison is blind" print identically. Its second 
#   file is tests-only at 139 added lines and the row's own exclude glob 
#   drops tests, so it adds ZERO bytes to the vendored file-set. THE PIN 
#   CANNOT ADVANCE BY REGENERATION IN ANY CASE: this tree does not 
#   reconstruct at f83d5aee, 1 of 17 hunks applying as measured in CM051 
#   #1878, and the regenerator refuses when the source has advanced past the 
#   pin, which it has by 55 commits. regenerate_forbidden STAYS TRUE 
#   alongside the ack without contradiction because the two answer different 
#   questions: the ack says the scrub's RESULT is already vendored, 
#   regenerate_forbidden says what a regeneration FROM source at the pinned 
#   sha would EMIT, and the pin is PRE-scrub. FIVE THINGS IN THE ARTEFACT: 
#   the cm048 producer re-vendored at CM048 53fcdf0b (#1881), which also took 
#   the vendored tree from 1142 undescribed divergence lines to zero; the 
#   cm041 producer grafted as ADDED LINES ONLY (#1884); the store-auth .pth 
#   import guard (#1886), net line delta zero; the reword that removed the 
#   operator identifier from the file gui/Makefile:1249 copies into the .app, 
#   plus its PR-time test (#1894), PROVEN DELIVERED by the v1.0.84 cut; and 
#   NEW FOR THIS CUT the hold_ack (#1896). THE DAEMON DOES NOT MOVE: 0.4.77 
#   at a9af0595, no re-pin, six pin sites untouched. EVERY SOURCE CHECKOUT ON 
#   THIS DISK WAS FETCHED BEFORE THE FRESHNESS GATE RAN, so a stale local 
#   clone could not make a lagging input read fresh: CM041, CM019, HR015, 
#   OS003 and CM051 all fetched, none moved, and CM041 origin/main reads 
#   a0f3ca1, the scrub commit itself, so the ack covers upstream HEAD for 
#   that path rather than a point behind it. THE WALK INSTRUMENT HAS MOVED 
#   EVEN THOUGH THE ARTEFACT HAS NOT: CM051 #1887, #1888 and #1890 are in the 
#   walk checkout and in no DMG, because gui/project.yml bundles 
#   box_walk_probes zero times, so a probe that moves because the instrument 
#   was wrong is a real move and it is not a product improvement. NOT 
#   FORECAST CLEAN: usage_journal_producers reaches 4 of 5 on the artefact 
#   alone and 5 only if the backfill #1890 kickstarts actually writes, which 
#   is the open question rather than a prediction; the two people probes turn 
#   on whether the re-sweep prunes the 21 vectors whose Person the graph no 
#   longer has, undetermined with the hydrate log absent; and the 
#   fact_missing residual is model behaviour. Under decision A the verdict 
#   rule stands.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

